Subject: [PATCH 0055] Bring-up checkpoints for the GPU attach (nmxtrace / nmxdrmdebug)

The first bare-metal test start on Wildcat Lake froze inside NMXGPU's attach: the last console line was
"NullMoth Intel: stolen memory 0x0, 64 MiB", xe printed nothing, and no log survived. This adds checkpoints so the
next test shows which step never returns. Everything is off unless the boot arguments are set; no driver logic changes.

- bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c (new): nmxtrace=1 prints "NMXT <step>" before each step; nmxtrace=2 also waits 200 ms
  so the line reaches the screen before a hang. nmxdrmdebug=<mask> sets drm.debug (e.g. 0x6 = driver + KMS).
- xnu/nmx_kext.cpp: checkpoints around the firmware wait, the driver hand-off and the framebuffer publish.
- bsdcompat/src/nmx_port.c: checkpoints around the device record, display pre-attach and the bus add (driver probe).
- fork_xe.py: a checkpoint before every statement-level call in xe_pci_probe, xe_device_probe_early and
  xe_device_probe (14 + 5 + 35).

Applies on top of 0051-0054.

